        "text_preview": "New York City Department of Environmental Protection · Bureau of Water Supply - Natural Resources Division · CARPENTERS EDDY EAST · Forest Management Project # 5116…",
        "extracted_text": "New York City Department of Environmental Protection\nBureau of Water Supply - Natural Resources Division\nCARPENTERS EDDY EAST\nForest Management Project # 5116\nNOTICE OF PROJECT AVAILABILITY\nDescription: The City of New York will sell 187 MBF of hardwood sawtimber and 89 cords of hardwood pulp through Carpenters Eddy East Forest Management Project #5116 in the Cannonsville watershed basin.\nSummary: This sale is comprised of mostly mature red oak and white ash. The project includes 2.5 miles of trail construction and 27 acres of shelterwood regeneration.\nProject Area: 103 ac\nTotal Volume: 187 MBF sawtimber and 89 cords hardwood pulp\nSpecies as a percent of total sawtimber volume: 49% Red Oak, 22% White Ash, 14% Red Maple, 9% Chestnut Oak.\nShow Dates: Prospective bidders should attend one of the public showings to receive the full bid package.\nBid Deadline: Sealed bids must be received by the date stated in the official notice.\nVolume by species (sawtimber MBF)\nSpecies\nSawtimber (MBF)\nPulp (cords)\nPercent of sawtimber\nRed Oak\n91.6\n28\n49%\nWhite Ash\n41.1\n18\n22%\nRed Maple\n26.2\n22\n14%\nChestnut Oak\n16.8\n12\n9%\nOther hardwoods\n11.3\n9\n6%\nTotal\n187.0\n89\n100%\nStand summary by unit\nStand\nAcres\nDominant species\nSawtimber (MBF)\nTreatment\n1\n28\nRed Oak\n62.4\nShelterwood\n2\n35\nWhite Ash / Red Oak\n71.2\nShelterwood\n3\n24\nRed Maple\n38.1\nGroup selection\n4\n16\nMixed hardwoods\n15.3\nTrail / access\nTotal\n103\n—\n187.0\n—",
